    "findings": "Both readers agreed on every category. The two related cyclamen illustrations show a single outlined body with short peripheral marks and upright stems. The paired outer f33v bodies have similar peripheral marks and join laterally at a shared stem; contact at the partly clipped third body is less clear. A round outlined organ with radiating marks can occur in Old World depictions, while this sample distinguishes the number and positions of the bodies. Calendula was coded thick-axis from the whole view and fine strands from the restricted region, showing scope sensitivity at a thick stem neck."
